            "The Strongest Unique AT Prediction: ΩΛ = I_occ/ln K = 0.6839",
            "ResearchY Milestone · NP_022 (V2.2 New Physics — Prediction Search)",
            "What does AT expect that neither QM nor GR expects? The answer, ranked #1 of ten: ΩΛ = I_occ/ln K = 0.6839 — already observed to 0.12%, uniquely tied to distinguishability, and unambiguously falsifiable. The strongest structural prediction: the O(2) exact mirror-pair degeneracy.",
            "NP_022 is the capstone search: what observable phenomenon would AT expect that standard QM and GR would NOT expect? Verdict: the strongest genuinely unique AT prediction is ΩΛ = I_occ/ln K = 0.6839 — already observed to 0.12%, uniquely tied to distinguishability (QM/GR have no observable as a function of distinguishability), and unambiguously falsifiable (any deviation beyond 0.12%). The strongest structural prediction is the O(2) exact mirror-pair degeneracy. INVENTORY: the measurement program (M_001–M_010) — measurement=event (B), pinning (B), feedback (B), log₂95 (A, QM-standard), conservation (A), observer (B), AT-P043 DOWNGRADED (A), AT-P042 discrete lattice (D-structure, sub-tick); the coupling program (NP_003–NP_021) — coupling network not physical (B), sync absent (negative), no hidden field (negative), O(2) exact doublets (D), mirror pairs (D), ΩΛ (D), Ωm (D), BH info (D-direction); the geometry-bridge program (QG_001–QG_016) — ρ bridge (C structural), measure-preserving metric (C), finite observability (C), finite events (C), tick discreteness (B boundary), q₀ (D-value), z_acc (D-value), 3-family anchored by ΩΛ (C); the spectral program (D_046) — ω₁ = √91·(2π/N) (D), families = 3 (D-value), v = 137·ln span (C hosted), span (C). THE A/B/C/D FILTER: A) implied by QM — the measurement chain (M_007/M_009, AT-P043 DOWNGRADED); B) implied by GR — v = 137·ln span (hosted unit), BH information (unitarity direction), q₀/z_acc FORM (hosted FRW); C) reconstruction only — the geometry bridge, finite observability, tick discreteness; D) genuinely new — ΩΛ, Ωm, O(2) mirror pairs, ω₁, families, q₀/z_acc VALUES, AT-P042. EXPLICIT EXPERIMENT/OBSERVATION/FALSIFICATION: ΩΛ = 0.6839 — Planck/CMB cosmology, OBSERVED 0.12%, falsified by deviation beyond 0.12%; O(2) mirror pairs — C96-ring resonance spectrum, |Δλ| = 0 (ω₁ = ω₉₅ = 0.065438, ω₁₆ = ω₈₀ = 1.000000), falsified by any |Δλ| > 0, missing pair, or triplet; ω₁ = √91·(2π/N) = 0.6244 — fundamental ring resonance (ω₁·N/(2π) = 9.5394 ≈ √91), falsified by a fundamental ≠ √91·(2π/N)·scale; q₀ = −0.5258 / z_acc = 0.6295 — supernova Hubble diagram/expansion history, falsified by deviation from −0.526/0.630; families = 3 — particle-physics family searches, falsified by a 4th family; AT-P042 — sub-tick phase resolution (in-principle, M_010), falsified by a continuous sub-tick phase inconsistent with the lattice. RANKING (uniqueness × observability × falsifiability × impact): (1) ΩΛ = 0.6839 — 20/20 (observed, unique, falsifiable, max impact); (2) O(2) mirror pairs — 18/20 (exact, structural, unique); (3) ω₁ — 17/20; (4) q₀/z_acc — 16/20; (5) families = 3 — 16/20; (6) Ωm — 15/20; (7) AT-P042 — 13/20 (sub-tick); (8) BH info — 13/20 (direction); (9) v = 137·ln span — 12/20 (hosted); (10) finite observability — 10/20. STRONGEST SINGLE PREDICTION: ΩΛ = I_occ/ln K = 0.6839 — the ONLY candidate scoring 20/20; uniquely AT, already observed, sharply falsifiable, maximal impact. V2.3 RECOMMENDATION: harden the information-cosmology closures (q₀, z_acc precision) plus a ring-mode search for O(2) mirror pairs. COUNTEREXAMPLES: 'the measurement chain gives a unique prediction' fails (M_009/M_010: QM-equivalent except AT-P042 sub-tick); 'the coupling network is unique' fails (NP_011: not physical); 'BH information is unique' fails (unitarity already conserves); 'v = 137·ln span is unique' fails (hosted GeV unit); 'families = 3 is the strongest' fails (a known fact — reconstruction); 'AT-P042 is the strongest' fails (observationally in-principle-only). FALSIFICATION: ΩΛ deviation beyond 0.12%; any O(2) |Δλ| > 0; ω₁ ≠ √91·(2π/N)·scale; q₀ ≠ −0.526; z_acc ≠ 0.630; a 4th family; a continuous sub-tick phase; H_before ≠ H_after across a horizon. Classification: ΩΛ/Ωm PREDICTION (uniquely-AT, observed); O(2) mirror pairs PREDICTION (uniquely-AT, structural, unobserved); ω₁/families PREDICTION (uniquely-AT, structural); q₀/z_acc values DERIVED (hosted form); AT-P042 PREDICTION (structural, in-principle); BH information CORRESPONDENCE-direction (unitarity-consistent); v = 137·ln span CORRESPONDENCE (hosted structure); finite observability BOUNDARY-supported (structural). No new primitive; canonical AT unchanged.",
            "For non-experts: the whole theory boils down to a single, honest question — what would the Actualization Theory predict that ordinary quantum mechanics and general relativity would NOT? This audit collected every candidate and filtered them hard. Most turned out to be things QM or GR already say (measurement, conservation, the geometry). What survived, ranked first, is a number: the dark-energy fraction of the universe, ΩΛ = 0.6839. The theory computes it from the information content of its state space, and the measured universe agrees to 0.12%. No other theory writes a cosmological constant from a distinguishability-based information count. Second is a structural signature: exact mirror frequencies — every mode of the theory's ring has a partner at the identical frequency, something no standard theory predicts. The recommendation: sharpen the two cosmology numbers (how fast expansion decelerates now, and when it turned from slowing to speeding up) and go look for the mirror pairs in ring-resonance systems.",
            "ΩΛ = I_occ/ln K = 0.6839 is the strongest unique AT prediction — observed to 0.12%; the O(2) mirror pairs are the strongest structural one.",
