        new(
            "researchy-qg013-three-family-origin",
            "The Three-Family Window Is a Confirmed Boundary — Anchored by the Observed ΩΛ",
            "ResearchY Milestone · QG_013 (V2.2 New Physics — Geometry Bridge)",
            "Why exactly three families? Not because pairing demands it (all octave rungs pair) and not because information is extremized (I_occ is monotone). The 3-family window is a confirmed boundary — anchored by the observed dark-energy fraction: N=96 is the unique pairing-complete rung reproducing ΩΛ = 0.6839.",
            "QG_013 asks why the observable sector consists of exactly three families. Verdict: the 3-family WINDOW is a CONFIRMED BOUNDARY — NOT reducible to distinguishability, count structure, or information density — but it is ANCHORED by the observed cosmology (ΩΛ = 0.6839). FAMILY-COUNT STRUCTURE: family count = floor(log₂(span))+1 is DERIVED (D_016); span(96) = 6.4025 is DERIVED (D_028); N=96 = 3·2⁵ is the octave rung (D_020/D_031); the family-count VALUE 3 at N=96 is DERIVED (two-level rule, D_040); the 3-family WINDOW (span ∈ [4,8)) is the BOUNDARY input. REMOVE THE 3-FAMILY ASSUMPTION — THE PAIRING TEST: the pairing-complete octave rungs 3·2^k are N=48 (2 families, span 3.240), N=96 (3, 6.403), N=192 (4, 12.779), N=384 (5, 25.537) — ALL have λ=12 mult 5 (complete pairing, verified exactly via the K=6 ring spectrum), so the Z2-paired complex sector (D_020) does NOT select 3 families (only the non-rungs N=64/128 fail pairing with λ=12 mult 1). INFORMATION DENSITY: I_occ (KL of the generation-share occupancy to uniform) is strictly MONOTONE increasing in N — 0.524 (N=48) → 0.630 (N=64) → 0.7513 (N=96) → 0.820 (N=128) → 1.013 (N=192) — there is NO information-theoretic extremum at N=96; 3 families does not minimize, maximize, or stationarize I_occ. THE OBSERVED-COSMOLOGY SELECTOR: ΩΛ = I_occ/ln K (ln K = 1.0986, K ≈ 3) is reproduced EXACTLY only by N=96 — ΩΛ(96) = 0.7513/1.0986 = 0.6839 (0.0% deviation, observed 0.12%); N=48 → 0.4773 (−30.2%), N=192 → 0.8153 (+19.2%), N=384 → 0.8945 (+30.8%). WHAT FIRST FAILS WHEN FAMILY COUNT ≠ 3: the OBSERVED COSMOLOGY — the predicted dark-energy fraction deviates by 19–31%, far beyond the 0.12% observational precision (the pairing-complete structure survives, the state capacity grows, but the information-density chain ΩΛ = I_occ/ln K deviates irrecoverably). DOES 3 EXTREMIZE AN INFORMATION QUANTITY? NO — I_occ is monotone increasing; 3 is selected by the OBSERVED ΩΛ = 0.6839, the one pairing-complete octave rung reproducing it. BOUNDARY REDUCTION TEST: reducible to the Z2-paired complex sector — NO (N=48/192/384 all pair); to count structure — NO (count same for every rung); to information density — NO (I_occ monotone); to the observed cosmology — YES as an ANCHOR, not a derivation (N=96 is the unique pairing-complete rung reproducing the observed ΩΛ). The 3-family window remains a BOUNDARY input (D_020/D_040) now ANCHORED by the information-cosmology chain. COUNTEREXAMPLES: 'pairing forces 3 families' fails (N=48/192/384 pair); 'I_occ is extremized at N=96' fails (monotone); 'the window is derived from information' fails (selected by OBSERVED ΩΛ); 'N=64/128 are alternative 3-family sectors' fails (they fail pairing); 'removing 3 families changes nothing' fails (every other rung off by 19–31%). FALSIFICATION: a derivation of the window from a deeper internal principle; a pairing-complete rung ≠ 96 reproducing ΩΛ = 0.6839; a measured ΩΛ ≠ I_occ(96)/ln K; a non-rung sector with decreasing I_occ. Classification: family-count VALUE 3 DERIVED (from span(96), D_016/D_046 P8); the 3-family WINDOW BOUNDARY (observable-sector input, confirmed D_020/D_040); N=96 DERIVED (octave rung); I_occ DERIVED (monotone, no extremum at 3); the observed ΩΛ = 0.6839 BOUNDARY (observed anchor); cosmology→family coupling DERIVED (ΩΛ selects the rung). No new primitive; canonical AT unchanged.",
            "For non-experts: why does nature have exactly three generations of matter — not two or four? This audit ran the test. It found that nothing inside the theory's own machinery forces the number three: every possible 'octave ring' — with two, three, four, or five families — can be made fully complex and reciprocal, so pairing does not decide. And the amount of information grows smoothly as the list grows, so three is not where information peaks or dips. What decides is the observed universe: the dark-energy fraction ΩΛ = 0.6839 that we measure is reproduced EXACTLY only by the three-family ring. Two families would give 0.48, four would give 0.82, five would give 0.89 — all wildly wrong. So the three-family window is a genuine input of the theory (a boundary), but it is not arbitrary: it is the one window consistent with what cosmology observes.",
