        new(
            "researchy-qg009-infinite-state-space-consistency",
            "The Infinite Is Consistent: Finiteness Fails Only at the Uniform Reference",
            "ResearchY Milestone · QG_009 (V2.2 New Physics — Geometry Bridge)",
            "Does an infinite distinguishable state space contradict physics? No — it is internally consistent, provided the count density converges. The geometric distribution sums to one exactly and carries finite entropy (2.0 bits). The only structure that breaks is the AT uniform-reference observable: there is no uniform measure on an infinite set.",
            "QG_009 asks whether an infinite distinguishable state space can support normalization, information, measurement, geometry, and gravity without contradiction. Verdict: YES — internally CONSISTENT when the count density is CONVERGENT (summable). KEY CONSTRUCTION: the geometric distribution ρ_k = (1−r)·r^k over k = 0,1,2,… satisfies Σρ_k = (1−r)/(1−r) = 1 EXACTLY (normalization survives, verified to machine precision) and carries finite Shannon entropy H = −log₂(1−r) − (r/(1−r))·log₂ r = 2.0 bits for r = 0.5 (closed form, numeric match); the power-law ρ_k ∝ k^(−2) normalizes via ζ(2) = 1.6449 with H ≈ 2.36 bits. NORMALIZATION: existence YES (geometric, power-law), uniqueness (many valid convergent families), stability (exact for fixed r) — only the UNIFORM assignment fails (Σ1 = ∞). INFORMATION: the CAPACITY log₂(N) diverges, but the realized entropy of a convergent infinite distribution is FINITE (2.0 bits geometric) — 'information breaks first' is REFINED. FIRST GENUINE FAILURE: the UNIFORM REFERENCE — a normalized uniform measure on a countably infinite set does not exist (Σc = c·∞ ∉ {0,1} for all c), so the AT observable I_occ = KL(ρ‖uniform) = 0.7513 nats (QG228) and ΩΛ = I_occ/ln K = 0.6839 (QG234) are ILL-DEFINED for infinite N. MEASUREMENT: Born weights Σ|ψ|² = Σρ = 1 exact for any convergent ρ; state identity coherent over infinite states. GEOMETRY: √(−g) = ρ (QG207) extends to any summable density — the conformal metric survives. DETERMINATION: A) finite required — NO (for generic consistency); B) finite emergent — NO; C) finite unnecessary — YES (required only for the AT uniform-reference information observable). PROVE/REFUTE: physics requires finite distinguishability — REFUTED as a generic necessity (a convergent infinite space is fully consistent across normalization, entropy, measurement, geometry, gravity); upheld only for the AT KL-to-uniform observable chain. This REFINES QG_008: 'information breaks first' holds for the uniform capacity and the AT KL observable, NOT for realized information content. COUNTEREXAMPLES: 'infinite states ⇒ information diverges' fails (H = 2.0 bits geometric); 'infinite states ⇒ no normalization' fails (Σ(1−r)r^k = 1 exactly); 'infinite states ⇒ no measurement' fails (Born weights sum to 1); 'infinite states ⇒ no geometry' fails (√(−g) = ρ extends to summable ρ); 'KL(ρ‖uniform) defined for infinite N' fails (no normalized uniform measure exists); 'QG_008 fully correct' — refined (only capacity and the AT KL observable break). FALSIFICATION: an infinite convergent ρ that cannot normalize; a convergent ρ with infinite entropy; an infinite construction forming KL-to-uniform; an infinite I_occ. Classification: finiteness BOUNDARY for the AT observable chain (I_occ, ΩΛ), NOT required for generic consistency; normalization Σρ = 1 DERIVED (exact for any convergent ρ); realized entropy H(ρ) DERIVED (finite for convergent ρ); capacity log₂(N) DERIVED (diverges — a capacity, not an observable); uniform reference REFUTED for infinite N; AT observable I_occ/ΩΛ BOUNDARY (finite-only); measurement/geometry/gravity DERIVED (survive any convergent ρ). No new primitive; canonical AT unchanged.",
            "For non-experts: does the theory need the list of distinguishable things to be finite? This audit found a surprising answer: NO — not for the physics itself. An infinite list can still be perfectly consistent, as long as the counts taper off (converge). A simple example — each possibility half as likely as the one before — adds up to exactly 100% and carries a finite, well-defined amount of information (2 bits). So an infinite world with tapering counts has working probabilities, working measurement, and working geometry. What actually breaks is something narrower: the theory's own information measure compares the real distribution to a 'perfectly uniform' one — but over an infinite list a perfectly uniform distribution cannot be made to sum to 100% (it sums to infinity). That comparison (and the cosmological constant built from it) only exists when the list is finite. So finiteness is not needed for the physics — it is needed for one specific observable that the theory derives. A refinement of the previous audit's 'information breaks first': the realized information is finite; only the uniform reference breaks.",
            "An infinite state space is internally consistent — only the uniform-reference observable (I_occ, ΩΛ) needs the finite list.",
            "“The infinite is coherent — what dies is the uniform dream.”",
            true,
            [
                new("ResearchY-QG_008", "FINITE DISTINGUISHABILITY AUDIT",
