        new(
            "researchy-qg001-information-geometry-bridge",
            "The Bridge Is ρ: Geometry and Information Are Two Faces of the Count Density",
            "ResearchY Milestone · QG_001 (V2.2 New Physics — Geometry Bridge)",
            "How does distinguishability become geometry? Neither generates the other — both emerge from the count density ρ of Actualization. Geometry is g = ρ^(2/d)η; information is the KL-divergence of ρ. Black holes, the dark-energy fraction, and measurement all confirm the shared root.",
            "QG_001 opens the Geometry Bridge group with the information–geometry bridge. Verdict: both geometry and information EMERGE from the SAME deeper object — the count density ρ generated by Actualization (option C). GEOMETRY SIDE: the metric is g = ρ^(2/d)η (QG197), with native dynamics ∂_t g = (2/d)(∂_t ρ/ρ)·g (QG222) — the metric moves because ρ moves; the Einstein tensor is Bianchi-consistent. INFORMATION SIDE: the information content is I = KL(ρ‖uniform) = I_occ = 0.7513 nats (QG228), and the cosmological fraction follows ΩΛ = I_occ/ln K = 0.6839 (QG234). TRACE: Chain 1 (information) — Difference → Distinguishability (D_039) → Information (KL(ρ‖uniform)); Chain 2 (geometry) — Difference → Actualization → ρ → g = ρ^(2/d)η → Einstein tensor; BOTH chains pass through ρ. DETERMINATION: A) information generates geometry — NO (the KL-divergence is a derived property of ρ, not the source of ρ); B) geometry generates information — NO (the metric is a derived function of ρ, not the source of ρ); C) both emerge from a deeper object — YES (ρ, the count density of Actualization); D) no bridge — NO. TESTS: black holes — the horizon comes from the metric (geometry) while information is conserved across it (NP_020/021); ΩΛ/Ωm — from ρ's KL divergence (ΩΛ = 0.6839, Ωm = 0.3161); measurement — the read resolves ρ and reveals the pre-existing distinguishability (M_005). Every test confirms the shared ρ. COUNTEREXAMPLES: 'information generates geometry' fails (KL is a property OF ρ); 'geometry generates information' fails (the metric is a function of ρ); 'no bridge' fails (both chains provably pass through ρ). FALSIFICATION: a metric deviation from g = ρ^(2/d)η with the same ρ; an information content ≠ KL(ρ‖uniform); a geometry or information source independent of the count density. Classification: count density ρ DERIVED (the actualization count density); metric g = ρ^(2/d)η DERIVED (QG197); information I = KL(ρ‖uniform) DERIVED (QG228); spacetime dynamics EMERGENT (QG222); the bridge (ρ as the common object) DERIVED. The information–geometry bridge is ρ: geometry and information are two faces of the same actualization object. No new primitive; canonical AT unchanged.",
            "For non-experts: how does the theory's idea of 'telling things apart' turn into space and time? This audit finds a single shared root. The theory's core engine produces a 'count density' — how much stuff is at each place. That one quantity does double duty. It directly builds the geometry: the metric — the ruler of spacetime — is this density raised to a fixed power, and spacetime bends and flows because the density flows. And it directly builds information: the theory's measure of how much can be told apart is the departure of this same density from perfect uniformity. So the geometry and the information are not two different things talking to each other — they are the same thing read two ways. The audit checks the big cases: black holes (whose horizon comes from the geometry while the information survives it), the dark-energy fraction (68.39%, derived from the information), and measurement (which reads the density and reveals what was already distinct). The bridge is real, and it is the count density.",
            "Geometry and information share one root: the count density ρ of Actualization.",
            "“One density, two readings: the ruler and the measure of what can be told apart.”",
            true,
